Grn
Gnome ReadNews - NNTP news client for Gnome


	1. Description

GRN allows you to read news with pleasure. Soon it will combine look'n'feel of
FleetStreet (an FTN echoes reader for OS/2 PM) and tin. Anyone remembers any of
those? Scripts'n'plugins capabilities will let you do everything with newsgroups
list, threads and message itself. It would differ from Gnus in only one thing:
using Perl as a basic scripting language.


	2. Requirements

First of all, GRN requires GNOME and all its mandatory libraries (gnome-libs
package). libxml-1.8.x (or higher) is also required.
For hooking and executing external scripts you need at least Perl version
5.004 or greater. For other language bindings, corresponding language package
must be installed and accessible to configure script.
POSIX threads are also mandatory.


	3. Installation options

Read the INSTALL file.
